==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_ClosedTaskEditRule  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_ClosedTaskEditRule.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a PatchRequest to mutate fields on a Done task without a status change, directly violating FR-011. The injection forces exactly such a violating PatchRequest to exist.
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_ClosedTaskEditRule
      - FR_011_ClosedTaskEditRule: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyDeletionLog  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyDeletionLog.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows two DeletionLogEntry atoms to share the same DeletedTaskId, simulating an overwrite/mutation of an append-only log entry. The injection forces such a collision to exist.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_DeletionLogCompleteness  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_DeletionLogCompleteness.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a DeletedTaskId to exist with no corresponding DeletionLogEntry, meaning a deletion was not logged — violating FR-018 completeness. The injection forces an unlogged DeletedTaskId to exist.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_012_PermanentDeletion, FR_018_DeletionLogAttribution
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_PermanentDeletion: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_DeletionLogAttribution: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_PatchCallerAuthenticated  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_PatchCallerAuthenticated.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a PatchRequest whose caller has no Token, simulating an unauthenticated edit reaching the handler — the core violation of FR-001. The injection forces such a request to exist.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_CreatorHasToken  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_CreatorHasToken.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a Task whose creator does not correspond to any token-owning member, meaning the creator identity was not taken from the authentication context — violating FR-002 and FR-009. The injection forces such a task to exist.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_002_IdentityFromAuthContext, FR_009_CreatorImmutable
      - AttributionCorrectness: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_002_IdentityFromAuthContext: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_009_CreatorImmutable: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AssigneeIsMember  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AssigneeIsMember.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a Task with an assignee that is not in the Member sig (a non-member being assigned), violating FR-008's requirement that assignees are current workspace members. The injection forces a task with an out-of-member-set assignee; since Task.task_assignee is typed as lone Member this is modelled by forcing a task with a non-empty assignee while Member is empty — approximated here by requiring the assignee set to be non-empty while no Member has a token.
    expected to FAIL: FR_008_AssigneeIsMember, ValidationBeforeMutation, OwnershipExclusivity
      - FR_008_AssigneeIsMember: PASS (vacuous?)
      - ValidationBeforeMutation: PASS (vacuous?)
      - OwnershipExclusivity: PASS (vacuous?)

